#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|chapter=His Own People|page=6|passage=It was flood-tide along Fifth Avenue; motor, brougham, and victoria swept by on the '''glittering''' current; pretty women glanced out from limousine and tonneau; young men of his own type, silk-hatted, frock-coated, the crooks of their walking sticks tucked up under their left arms, passed on the Park side.}}
